  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "The University of Maryland, Baltimore County (UMBC) is a public research university in Catonsville, Maryland, founded in 1966. Known as an \"Honors University,\" it is highly regarded for its STEM programs (particularly computer science and engineering), high research activity (R1), and national leadership in innovation and undergraduate teaching. Key Details About UMBC: Student Population: Roughly 13,000–14,000 students (undergraduate and graduate). Rankings: Frequently ranked among the top 100 most innovative schools and top national universities by U.S. News & World Report. Focus Areas: Strong emphasis on science, engineering, information technology, public policy, and human services. Location: Suburban campus located near Baltimore and approximately 45 minutes from Washington, D.C.. Athletics: Competes in NCAA Division I as the UMBC Retrievers in the America East Conference. UMBC is part of the University System of Maryland and is recognized for its diverse community and commitment to inclusive excellence in education.",
